# Benchmark fixtures record an immutable sha256 source_digest over their
# exact bytes (core/schemas/benchmark-fixture-manifest.schema.json) - that
# digest is only reproducible across machines if every checkout produces
# identical bytes. Without this, core.autocrlf=true (a common Windows git
# default) converts these files to CRLF on checkout while the git blob
# itself stays LF, so a fresh Windows clone's source_digest would never
# match what was recorded (Linux/CI checkouts never convert, so this
# never surfaced there) - a real bug found via `eifctl_benchmark.py
# validate-manifest` failing after a routine `git rebase` on Windows.
docs/benchmarks/fixtures/** text eol=lf
